+
+[356374](https://forums.developer.nvidia.com/t/moving-from-mac-to-nvidia-bought-powerful-hardware-but-drowning-in-configs/356374) is a memory-admission corroboration only: an owner reports vLLM/Nemotron 30B reaching ~110 GB allocation and a Qwen3-VL 235B filling a single Spark such that companion models cannot run. The thread gives no host-freeze/OOM timeline or cause isolation, so it does not establish a new failure signature. The later community launcher starts selectable LLM/reranker/embed/OCR/Whisper services with fixed contexts and no aggregate memory admission estimate; it may print “All servers started” after readiness loops time out. This is an unverified external script, not evidence of a BB defect. Use exact workload/cgroup pressure tests already specified here; do not treat 110 GB or one model list as a universal threshold.
