+**`BB-GRIDBOOK-COLD-LOAD-UMA-BALLOON`** — [377773, posts 55–70 and 77](https://forums.developer.nvidia.com/t/exciting-new-enhancements-to-prismaquant-gridbook/377773/55) reports a repeated Spark OOM/SIGTERM while cold-loading an 83.22 GiB Laguna/Gridbook model. The author says the clean-boot host began with 118 GiB available, then vLLM logged ~29–30 GiB available, `nvidia-smi` showed one EngineCore at 87,446 MiB, host `top` showed ~121 GiB used with swap nearly exhausted, and dmesg recorded OOM. The attempt used context 262144 and `gpu_memory_utilization=.85`; it also failed at 32K, with both eugr and vanilla vLLM, fresh boot, and Gridbook .6/.7. The plugin author acknowledged a memory-balloon bug in an earlier release, but its version and connection to this reproduction are unproven. Gate exact cold-load UMA headroom from live RAM/swap/cgroup/RSS/GPU observations, timestamp each counter, and preserve remote logs; do not turn this report’s flag or context into universal limits. Pastebins, images and external repositories remain unread.
