+**`BB-LING-VLLM-RSS-DRIFT-OOM`** — [377903, posts 47–49](https://forums.developer.nvidia.com/t/ant-ling-3-0-flash-124b-a5b-new-fast-model-for-one-spark/377903/47) report another user’s Ling INT4/vLLM workload growing host memory to OOM in about 20 minutes while KV cache reportedly stays at 5%; that owner later removes the service after long-context decode slowdown. Exact image, vLLM commit, request pattern, RSS/cgroup/swap timeline and OOM logs are absent, so the source does not prove a Ling or vLLM leak. Track process/cgroup RSS and host/swap pressure separately from KV use through a sustained exact-stack canary, retain evidence off-host, and bound admission before OOM.
